  "term": "divalproex sodium",
  "definition": "Divalproex sodium is a chemical form of valproate used for anticonvulsant and antiepileptic effects. In the body it separates to valproate ion and may reduce seizure-related nerve activity by increasing brain GABA and by limiting repetitive neuronal firing through effects on sodium channels.",
